Package: lagdynamics
Title: Lag Sequential Analysis, Dynamics, and Lag Transition Networks
Version: 0.34.1
Authors@R:
    c(person("Mohammed", "Saqr", email = "saqr@saqr.me",
             role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
             comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-5881-3109")),
      person("Sonsoles", "López-Pernas", role = "aut",
             comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-9621-1392")))
Description: Implements lag sequential analysis of categorical event and
    sequence data. For each ordered pair of states it tests whether one state
    follows another at a given lag more or less often than expected under
    independence, reporting adjusted residuals, transitional probabilities and
    Yule's Q in tidy data frames. Five test engines are provided (classical,
    two-cell, bidirectional, parallel dominance and non-parallel dominance).
    Transitions can be evaluated with bootstrap intervals, analytic certainty,
    split-half reliability, case-drop stability and permutation tests, and
    groups compared by permutation or by a Bayesian Dirichlet-multinomial
    contrast. Supports long-format event logs, sequence objects, multiple lags,
    structural zeros, transition and initial probabilities, plots of lag
    transition networks, and a directed transfer-entropy measure. The method
    follows Sackett and others (1979) <doi:10.3758/BF03205679>.
